Based on your description, three possible causes come to mind;

1.  Atopic dermatitis or eczema: This is a chronic skin condition that can cause red, itchy, and inflammatory skin lesions. It can affect the ear canal and occur in response to exposure to potential allergens or irritants in the environment.(allergied?)

2.  Contact dermatitis: This is a skin reaction that occurs when the skin comes into contact with an allergen or irritant. It can cause redness, itching, and blistering, and can occur in the ear canal in response to exposure to certain substances in the environment.
